#!/bin/sh
# Fail fast when the Pi registry password isn't exported.
#
# Kamal runs this before every deploy-family command (deploy / redeploy / rollback / setup) and
# aborts the run if it exits non-zero. Without it, an unset variable becomes an empty password and
# the push fails deep inside the build with a 401 from the registry.
#
# This has to be a hook, not a line in .kamal/secrets: that file is parsed by dotenv, which can't
# honour ${VAR:?} and never aborts on an empty value. A hook runs in a real shell, so ${VAR:?}
# (fires on unset OR empty) does the job and its non-zero exit stops the deploy.
: "${KAMAL_REGISTRY_PASSWORD:?is not set — export the Pi registry htpasswd password (user stash) before deploying}"
